OL,3,GNEWSAHospital to pilot Hugh's Law after
OL,4,Adeath of boy, 6
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe parents of a boy who died of cancer
OL,7,Fand a new children's hospital will work
OL,8,Ftogether to shape how families of
OL,9,Fseriously ill children are supported by
OL,10,Fthe NHS.
OL,12,FCeri and Frances Menai-Davis, from
OL,13,FHertford, lost their son Hugh, 6, in
OL,14,F2021, and have since been campaigning
OL,15,Ffor Hugh's Law, which would provide
OL,16,Fpaid leave for carers and guarantee job
OL,17,Fsecurity.
OL,19,FTheir charity, It's Never You, is part
OL,20,Fof a pilot with the Cambridge
OL,21,FChildren's Hospital (CCH), due to open
OL,22,Fin 2031.
OL,23,APub: 28-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
